# Lesson Design Rules

## Language (ORT Stage 2–3)
- 1–2 short sentences per story page
- Prefer sight words and previously taught vocabulary
- Sentence length: roughly 3–8 words; avoid complex clauses
- New words: max ~6–8 per lesson; introduce with picture + audio first
- Tone: friendly adventure; dragons OK if gentle and playful

## Required lesson structure
1. Cover (title, character, Start)
2. Vocabulary preview (picture + word; tap to hear)
3. Story pages (illustration + clickable words)
4. Comprehension quiz (instant correct/incorrect feedback + praise)
5. Sight-word practice (tap / match / say)
6. Follow-up notes for tutor/parent (checkboxes + comments; `localStorage`)

## Technical
- Single self-contained HTML per lesson (inline CSS/JS OK); shared assets only as images
- Pronunciation: Web Speech API (`speechSynthesis`), rate ~0.75–0.85, prefer en-US/en-GB child-friendly voice if available
- Tap any word → speak that word + highlight
- 「Read to me」→ read sentence by sentence with highlight sync
- Large fonts (story text ≥ 28px), big tap targets, high contrast
- UI suitable for a 5-year-old: big buttons, simple icons, short labels
- No external paid APIs; works offline once loaded (except first image load)

## Visuals
- Picture-book style illustrations, consistent character design across a lesson
- Store images in `lessons/assets/lesson-XX/`
- Alt text in English, simple

## Index
- Root `index.html` lists all lessons for the tutor with clear links and short descriptions
